<title>ITALY: Banca di Roma says sells Interbanca.</title>
<headline>Banca di Roma says sells Interbanca.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian bank Banca di Roma said on Thursday it had agreed to sell the entire share capital of its Interbanca unit to Antoniana PV for 625 billion lire ($385.4 million).</p>
<p>The deal was announced at a news conference by Banca di Roma chairman Cesare Geronzi. Antoniana is a bank based in northeastern Italy. ($ = 1621 Italian Lire)</p>
